<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-929] IgniteCache.close should not delete the cache from the cluster</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-929</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Need to introduce IgniteCache.destroy() method instead. close() method should be implemented differently for LOCAL and distributed caches&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;For LOCAL cache close() should be equivalent to destroyCache()&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;For distributed caches close(), if called on clients, should close client cache, but not destroy cache on the whole cluster.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;For distributed caches close(), if called on a server node, should be a no-op&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;TCK should run with LOCAL cache.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
